    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-m/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-m/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A curve C has equation − x y = e ln x , x &gt; 0 . a) Show that the x coordinate of the stationary point of C lies between 1 and 2 . ( ) 6 b) Use an iterative formula based on the Newton Raphson method to find the x coordinate of the stationary point of C , correct to 8 decimal places. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:593.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-m/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Differentiating e−x ln x gives −e−x ln x + e−x/x, hence y′ = e−x(1/x −ln x). [A1] Because e−x &gt; 0, set 1/x −ln x = 0, giving 1 −x ln x = 0. The source uses f = 1 −x ln x, with f(1) = 1 and f(2) = 1 −2 ln 2 = −0.386 . . .. Equivalently, the stationary equation is F(x) = x ln x −1 . [M1] = 0 The continuous F has F(1) = −1 [A1] and F(2) = 2 ln 2 −1 &gt; 0, [A1] so there is a root in (1, 2). [A1] As F is increasing for x ≥1 and negative for 0 &lt; x ≤1, it is the only stationary point. [A1] (b) By the Newton–Raphson method:\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-m/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The source differentiates f to get −[1 · ln x + x(1/x)] = −1 −ln x. Newton–Raphson then simplifies as follows: xn+1 = xn −f(xn) f′(xn) xn+1 = xn −1 −xn ln xn −1 −ln xn xn+1 = xn + 1 −xn ln xn 1 + ln xn xn+1 = xn + xn ln xn + 1 −xn ln xn 1 + ln xn xn + 1 xn+1 = 1 + ln xn Equivalently, apply xn+1 = xn −xn ln xn −1 [M1] [A1] 1 + ln xn\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-m/q8-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"starting at x1 = 1.5. [A1] This gives x2 ≈1.778770590, x3 ≈1.763266078, x4 ≈1.763222835, then x5 ≈1.763222834. [A1] One more application gives x6 = 1.763222834 . . ., confirming the stable digits: Thus x = 1.76322283 [A1] to eight decimal places: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
