      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-m/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The graph has vertex (3, 4). Intersection with the levels 8, 13, 20 requires respectively (x −3)2 = 4, 9, 16. Since f(x) = (x −3)2 + 4, the three equations have unrestricted root pairs {1, 5}, {0, 6} and {−1, 7}, respectively: [M1] The domain must include 1 and 5, include exactly one of 0 and 6, and exclude −1, 7. [A1] Including 0 and excluding 6 gives the maximal interval (−1, 6) ; [M1] [A1] including 6 and excluding 0 gives (0, 7) . [A1] In the first case 0 ∈(−1, 6); in the second 6 ∈(0, 7). [A1] Source clarification. The printed conditions alone allow many smaller domains: The handwritten working gives the maximal intervals, which are listed above:\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
